{#- Oxidized (formulas/oxidized, on monitoring): which network devices it
   backs up, and whether it runs at all. Imported by pillar/oxidized.sls
   (the data), pillar/homepage.sls (its tile), pillar/prometheus.sls (fetch
   check) and pillar/backup.sls (its local repo) — one place for the checks,
   so the four can't disagree.

   A device is in `devices` only when its pillar data is complete (host,
   pinned SSH host key) AND its SSH key resolves from OpenBao
   (homelab/oxidized/<name>, key `ssh_key`). Oxidized refuses to start with
   zero devices ("source returns no usable nodes"), so `enabled` also needs
   one — plus the Forgejo deploy key (homelab/oxidized/forgejo), without
   which the history would never leave monitoring. Until then nothing about
   Oxidized exists anywhere.

   device_defs: name -> model (Oxidized model name), host (IP), username
   (read-only device account), port (SSH, default 22), host_key ({enc, key}
   from `ssh-keyscan <host>` — public data; Oxidized verifies it,
   input.ssh.secure). FRITZ!Box and the Omada switches have no Oxidized
   model — formulas/oxidized README "Devices".

   opnsense: no OPNsense box is in inventory.md yet — set host and host_key
   once it exists (README "OPNsense"). #}
{%- set device_defs = {
    'opnsense': {
        'model': 'opnsense',
        'host': '',
        'username': 'oxidized',
        'port': 22,
        'host_key': {},
    },
} %}

{%- set devices = {} %}
{%- for name, d in device_defs | dictsort %}
{%-   set key = salt['sdb.get']('sdb://osvault/homelab/data/oxidized/' ~ name ~ '?ssh_key') or '' %}
{%-   if d.host and d.host_key and key is string and key | length > 0 and not key.startswith('sdb://') %}
{%-     set dev = d.copy() %}
{%-     do dev.update({'ssh_key': key}) %}
{%-     do devices.update({name: dev}) %}
{%-   endif %}
{%- endfor %}

{%- set forgejo_key = salt['sdb.get']('sdb://osvault/homelab/data/oxidized/forgejo?ssh_key') or '' %}
{%- set forgejo_key_pub = salt['sdb.get']('sdb://osvault/homelab/data/oxidized/forgejo?ssh_key_pub') or '' %}
{%- set forgejo_ok = forgejo_key is string and forgejo_key | length > 0 and not forgejo_key.startswith('sdb://') %}

{%- set oxidized = {
    'enabled': forgejo_ok and devices | length > 0,
    'devices': devices,
    'forgejo_key': forgejo_key,
    'forgejo_key_pub': forgejo_key_pub,
    'host_port': 8888,
    'url': 'http://192.168.178.25:8888',
} %}
